source is UTF-8, and a literal holds what it says
  héllo wörld
  日本語
  Ελληνικά

a name is written in any script, and so is an operator
  héllo wörld, 日本語 テキスト, ελληνικά κείμενο
  6 × 7 = 42
  evens ∪ odds = [1, 2, 3, 4]

a char is a UTF-16 code unit, so this one is two
  😀: 2 chars, 1 point
  escaped and literal agree: true
  \u20AC is €, \u0041cat is Acat

every .NET encoding is reachable, here for né
  UTF-8    6E C3 A9
  UTF-16   6E 00 E9 00
  UTF-32   6E 00 00 00 E9 00 00 00

normalization comes from .NET too
  \u00E9 is 1 char, e\u0301 is 2
  composed =~ decomposed is false
  after NFC it is true
